         <div type="bio">
            <p>Publisher, born in England, but made his name in Paris. With <name type="person" key="babo75">Henri Babou</name>, he published JJ’s <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Haveth Childers Everywhere</name> (1930), distributed in the United States by Elbridge Adams’s Fountain Press. The following year Kahane established the Obelisk Press, which in 1932 published a limited edition of <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Pomes Penyeach</name> decorated with initial letters designed by <name type="person" key="joyc07">Lucia Joyce</name>. The Obelisk Press became widely known for its avant-garde list. <hi rend="bold">William Brockman</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
